Certified training curricula/training modules on FLA service provisions</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- 2 new FLA Centers established and operational respectively in Gjirokastra and Vlora judicial districts.
- Two specific training modules on Free Legal Aid Guaranteed by the State developed and delivered to MoJ/Directorate of Free Legal Aid. These training modules were institutionalized through partnerships with the Albanian School for Public Ad-ministration (ASPA) for Primary Legal Aid Service and the National Chamber of Advocates of Albania/School of Advocacy (NCHA) for Secondary Legal Aid Service.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">6 functional Legal Free Aid Centers;
Network of service providers established and functional in the selected areas;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Pogradec, Lezha, Durres, Shkodra, Peshkopi and Fier FLA Centers are operational.
- Increased FLA provision to marginalized women and men: A total of 1322 persons received free legal aid. 568 persons with low or no income benefited the most from these services.
- Strengthened partnership with CSOs, People&#x2019;s Advocate and Commissioner for Protection from Discrimination for better referral of cases at local level and expanding outreach to remote areas and marginalized women and men.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
